# Flecha: in a tab a coding agent drives, only the shell's scripts run. chrome.flechaPrivate.setAgentTab() marks the tab (FlechaAgentTab, which hands the mark to the page that replaces a discarded one). Each frame gets the mark as it is created, and a child frame made in its parent's process starts with its parent's mark. The renderer then skips other extensions' content scripts and executeScript() calls there. A password manager's frames (Proton Pass adds them to every page) would otherwise stop the shell's debugger from driving the page, since Chromium keeps one extension's debugger out of a page holding another extension's frame. Chromium's debugger checks are unchanged.
